<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">José Núñez de Cáceres</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1772–1846</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">José Núñez de <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caceres">Cáceres</a> was a Dominican lawyer and official who, frustrated by Spanish neglect, led a bloodless coup in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santo-domingo">Santo Domingo</a> on 1 December 1821. He proclaimed the Independent State of Spanish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haiti">Haiti</a> and sought union with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/esztergom">Gran</a> Colombia. The state ended when Haitian forces under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jean-pierre-boyer">Jean-Pierre Boyer</a> occupied the country in February 1822.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jose-nunez-de-caceres.jpg" alt="José Núñez de Cáceres" width="298" height="318" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown/Desconocido · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nunezcaceres.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
